# p_7c3f — Omar's afternoon departure: wallet, shoes, scarf, and phone go out at 1:40

Omar works afternoon-to-night shifts (roughly 1:40 pm to 11 pm). In the morning he is home, mostly in the kitchen (the robot finds him there from midnight through 8 am). Around noon he starts getting ready to leave: his wallet moves from the entry floor to the entry table, his shoes come off the rack and land on the entry floor, his scarf drops from the wardrobe to the entry hook, and his phone ends up on the coffee table. By 1:40 he walks out with all of them. His cycling gear (bike lock, helmet) does NOT go with him — it stays at the entry all day, confirming he does not cycle to work. His tablet also stays home at the nightstand.

This document is distinguished by its specific pre-departure staging locations (entry_table for wallet, entry_floor for shoes, entry_hook for scarf, coffee_table for phone) and by the claim that these four items are OUT_OF_HOUSE from about 13:40 until 23:00 on weekdays. It is refuted if any of those four items is sighted inside the house during 14:00–22:00 on a weekday, or if the staging locations are consistently wrong (e.g., wallet always at entry_floor rather than entry_table in the 12–13:40 window).

