# p_e91b — Omar's tablet is a nightstand device; it never goes to the kitchen chair or to work

The robot's sightings place Omar's tablet at the nightstand_b1 on 3 of 4 weekday 9–17 h looks, and the one "miss" was actually the tablet being at the nightstand when the mixture predicted the kitchen chair. Omar's tablet is a personal bedroom device — he reads or watches things in bed in the early morning (he is in the kitchen 00:00–08:00, so the tablet sits on the nightstand while he is up and about, then he might grab it before bed). It is NOT a kitchen-table companion, and it is NOT taken to his afternoon-to-night shift.

